# Shared UI and i18n

## Do

- Keep `packages/ui` **framework-agnostic**: do not import `next-intl` or read app message catalogs inside `@metaboost/ui`.
- Pass **all** user-visible strings, `aria-label`, `title`, empty states, and loading text from the app via props.
- When adding new copy-bearing props, add keys to `apps/web` and/or `apps/management-web` `i18n/originals/en-US.json` and keep other locales in sync (see **i18n** skill and **i18n-locale-language** rule).

## Do not

- Do not hardcode English — or any single locale — in shared components as **defaults** for text that end users or assistive tech will see.
- Do not add “temporary” English defaults in `@metaboost/ui` to save app wiring; wire the app instead.

## Review checklist

- Any new string literal in `packages/ui` shown in the UI or read by AT → move to app props.
- Formatting with ICU variables (`{name}`) stays in app `t(...)` calls, not inside `@metaboost/ui`.
